WEBVTT

00:00:26.888 --> 00:00:30.718
Very few trees can compete 
with this carbon impact,

00:00:30.718 --> 00:00:37.009
but today, humanity produces more 
than 1,400 tons of carbon every minute.

00:00:37.009 --> 00:00:38.709
To combat climate change,

00:00:38.709 --> 00:00:42.249
we need to steeply reduce 
fossil fuel emissions,

00:00:42.249 --> 00:00:47.106
and draw down excess CO2 
to restore our atmosphere’s balance

00:00:47.106 --> 00:00:49.196
of greenhouse gases.

00:00:49.196 --> 00:00:52.026
But what can trees do to help
in this fight?

00:00:52.026 --> 00:00:55.586
And how do they sequester carbon 
in the first place?

00:00:55.586 --> 00:00:59.116
Like all plants, trees consume
atmospheric carbon

00:00:59.116 --> 00:01:02.086
through a chemical reaction 
called photosynthesis.